，果断的拒绝了，村长家虽然有钱，但是家大业大，家里人口也多，若是太过依赖他们家，日后凡儿过去日子定不好过，若是家里条件不是这般的差，都不该应下收村长家给的银子。但是若家里条件再好一点，又怎会让凡儿去他家当童养媳呢？贾氏越想越揪心，都怪自己太过无能……“娘，你别忧心了，是我自己答应的，而且也没什么不好的呀，我要从小培育自己的相公，让他对我服服帖帖的，嘿嘿。”苏小凡咧唇一笑，虽然成为童养媳或许会招他人讥笑，但是总比顶着被退婚了日后再没人要的名头要好吧，而且来日方长，此为也不过是为了度过眼下的难关罢了。想自己才刚来这里，身子又弱，娘亲又临盆在即，能有一笔银子救急下，又何乐而不为。若是日后自己有了别的喜欢的男子，又或是这小宝贝儿长大了有了中意的女子，再来商议对策好了，今日收了他们的银子，来日也是可以还回去的，只要过了眼前这一关，一定可以想到办法赚钱的。“服服帖帖？”萧遗墨挑眉看着她，稚嫩的小脸上布满怒容。“可不是嘛，一个好男人，就是要疼老婆的。”苏小凡起身拎了水桶，朝屋后的一口水井走去。“那可不是服服帖帖的意思。”萧遗墨紧跟而去。“……”苏小凡决定不再跟他说下去，这小宝贝儿似乎真的很早熟，理解能力也超强，难道是传说中的神童来着？“哦……这口井真不错。”生活在大城市中的苏小凡这是第一次见到古井，在这即将步入夏天的季节里，靠近井边竟觉得有些许凉，若是在炎热的夏日，来这里乘凉估计不错。萧遗墨白了她一眼，大惊小怪的，难道她这是第一次见到自家的井？苏小凡将桶栓在绳子上，慢慢放下去，然后费了九牛二虎之力将水桶弄了上来，到水面上的时候，桶里已经只剩下一半水了，回头看了下身后的路，顿时打消了将水拎回去的念头，这就算拎回去，也只剩下一点点了呀。往日似乎都是娘跟奶奶负责打水的，她们究竟是如何将水打回去然后做饭的？“小宝贝儿，不要靠近井边哦，我去将野菜拿来这里清洗，你在这等我。”苏小凡认真的对着他交代了一番，才转身离去，等洗好了菜，再来多跑几次，打水煮吧。萧遗墨对着她的背影怒火：“别把小爷我当小孩子对待。”苏小凡并未回头，笑着嘀咕，本来就是小孩子不是吗？一通忙活，当苏小凡做好吃的，天都已经全黑了，叶氏找了一些石头，将缺了一小截腿的桌子垫平整来，苦恼的看着屋内几个不能坐的凳子，将唯一一个能坐的递给了萧遗墨说：“小少爷，坐吧，我们站着吃就可以了。”萧遗墨努努嘴：“小爷我也可以站着吃。”他觉得，这家人一定是有史以来自己见过的最穷的。“你就坐着吧，站着不够高啊。”苏小凡直接将他抱起来放在了凳子上坐着。“你……”萧遗墨怒急，但是却又无可奈何，自己的身高站着的确是不好吃饭。“凡儿这是跟谁学的，很香。”贾氏拿着饭勺给众人盛满野菜粥，虽然还未吃，问着味道就让人很有食欲。苏小凡笑笑：“自学的，锅里剩下的粥就不多了，所以就加了野菜跟小宝贝儿先前采的野蘑菇，做成了野菜粥，这样大家都有粥喝了，虽然野菜多了点……”“很好吃啊。”叶氏吃了一口后，惊叹出声，从小便开始吃野菜了，也吃过各种做法的，但是这碗野菜粥一定是自己吃过的最好吃的。“的确是，真不敢相信这是野菜做出来的。”贾氏尝后也是跟叶氏一般的反应。苏小凡吃了几口，倒是觉得味道很普通，但是跟记忆中她们往日所吃的东西比起来，这确实是好了很多，看来日后得想想办法改善改善家里的生活水平，首要的就是得想办法赚钱。萧遗墨拧着眉，看着碗中野菜，纠结了半天后，闭上眼，扒了一大口到嘴里，原本是打算直接吞咽下去的，但是入口后，奇迹般的感觉并不那么糟，又吃了几口后说：“味道还不错。”“那就多吃点，锅里还有哦，吃饱饱的才能长得高。”苏小凡笑着拍了拍他的头。“都说别拿小爷当小孩子了。”萧遗墨瞪了她一眼，心中烦躁，哪是多吃就能长高那么简单的事儿啊。“呵呵，好……”", "source": "www.quanwenyuedu.io", "source_url": "https://www.quanwenyuedu.io/n/chongfuchengyin-nongjiatongyangxi/6.html", "_fixed": true, "content_en": "Chapter 6 Wild Vegetable Porridge Su Xiaofan took Xiao Yimo's hand and said, \"Baby, let's go back. When we feel better tomorrow, we can go up the mountain again. People say that you rely on the mountain to live on the mountain. There must be many treasures on this mountain. Tomorrow, sister, I will take you to hunt for treasures.\" \"You are my wife, not my sister, and you are not allowed to call me honey. It's annoying.\" Xiao Yimo glared at her, broke away from her hand, and walked down the mountain. Su Xiaofan quickly kept up with him, with a smile on his face, and didn't care about his anger at all. Children, generally speaking, what they say they hate may not really mean they hate him. After returning home, Su Xiaofan used the young grass to make a small nest in a corner of the main room, put the little rabbits in it, and then carried a basket of wild grass into the kitchen. Mrs. Jia came out of the house and saw Xiao Yimo squatting on the ground, looking at the baby rabbits in the nest. After scanning around, he remembered that several small round stools in the house had been taken away. He pointed to Su Xiaofan's room and said softly to him: \"If the young master is tired, go to Fan'er's room to rest.\" Xiao Yimo raised his eyes, his bright black eyes were unusually calm. He nodded lightly and stood up and walked towards the kitchen. Jia also entered the kitchen, looked at Su Xiaofan who was sorting the wild vegetables and said, \"Go get some water for mother.\" Su Xiaofan stopped what he was doing and glanced at the empty bucket beside him. He suddenly felt weak all over. Can the bucket full of holes really lift water? \"It's better to go to my house and get a good bucket.\" Xiao Yimo was also confused like her. The bucket was definitely leaking even before it was carried to the kitchen. Even if it was left, there wouldn't be much water left. \"No need, how dare I bother your family again.\" Mrs. Jia refused without thinking. Although the village chief's family is rich, they have a big business and a large family. If they rely too much on their family, Fan'er's life will not be easy in the future. If the family's conditions are not so bad, they should not accept the money given by the village chief's family. But if the family's conditions were better, how could Fan'er be allowed to become a child bride in his family? The more Jia thought about it, the more worried she became, blaming herself for being too incompetent... \"Mom, don't worry, I made the promise myself, and there's nothing wrong with it. I want to nurture my husband from an early age and make him obedient to me, hehe.\" Su Xiaofan grinned. Although becoming a child bride might attract ridicule from others, it was better than bearing a name that no one would want in the future after the engagement was broken off. Moreover, the future was long, so this was just to get through the current difficulties. I thought that I had just come here, I was weak, and my mother was about to give birth, so why not do it if I could have a sum of money to help me in an emergency. If you have another man you like in the future, or if this little baby grows up and has a woman you like, you can discuss the countermeasures. The money you collected from them today can be paid back in the future. As long as you pass this hurdle, you will definitely be able to find a way to make money. \"Be obedient?\" Xiao Yimo looked at her with raised eyebrows, his young face full of anger. \"Isn't that right? A good man loves his wife.\" Su Xiaofan stood up, picked up the bucket, and walked towards a well behind the house. \"That doesn't mean being submissive.\" Xiao Yimo followed closely. \"...\" Su Xiaofan decided not to talk to him anymore. This little baby seems to be really precocious and has super understanding ability. Could he be a legendary child prodigy? \"Oh... this well is really nice.\" This is the first time Su Xiaofan, who lives in a big city, has seen an ancient well. In this season, which is about to enter the summer, it feels a little cool to be close to the well. If it is a hot summer day, it is probably a good idea to come here to enjoy the coolness. Xiao Yimo rolled his eyes at her, making a fuss. Could this be the first time she saw her well? Su Xiaofan tied the bucket to the rope, lowered it slowly, and then spent a lot of effort to get the bucket up. When it reached the surface, there was only half of the water left in the bucket. He looked back at the road behind him and immediately gave up the idea of ​​carrying the water back. Even if he carried it back, there would only be a little left. In the past, my mother and grandma seemed to be responsible for fetching water. How did they fetch the water back and cook? \"Little baby, don't go near the well. I'm going to bring the wild vegetables here to wash them. You wait for me here.\" Su Xiaofan explained to him seriously before turning around and leaving. After the vegetables are washed, he will run a few more times to fetch water and boil them. Xiao Yimo was angry at her back: \"Don't treat me like a child, young master.\" Su Xiaofan didn't look back and murmured with a smile, he is a child in the first place, isn't he? After a busy day of work, when Su Xiaofan was preparing delicious food, it was already dark. Ye found some stones and flattened the table with a small leg missing. He looked at the several unsitable stools in the room distressedly and handed the only one that could be sat on to Xiao Yimo and said, \"Sit down, young master. We can eat standing up.\" \"Just sit, it's not high enough to stand.\" Su Xiaofan directly picked him up and put him on a stool to sit. \"You...\" Xiao Yimo was angry, but he was helpless. It was really difficult for him to eat while standing at his height. \"Who did Fan'er learn this from? It's very fragrant.\" Jia took a rice spoon and filled everyone with wild vegetable porridge. Although they hadn't eaten it yet, asking about the taste made people very appetizing. Su Xiaofan smiled and said, \"I am a self-taught porridge. There was not much porridge left in the pot, so I added wild vegetables and the wild mushrooms that my little baby picked earlier to make porridge. This way everyone can have porridge to drink, even though there are a little too many wild vegetables...\" \"It's delicious.\" After taking a bite, Ye exclaimed. He has been eating wild vegetables since he was a child, and he has tried various ways of making it, but this bowl of wild vegetable porridge must be the best he has ever tasted. \"Indeed, I can't believe it.", "title_en": "Chapter 6"}